Some last minute reminders generated by the AI that did all the coding:

Files:

index.html, styles.css, game.js — the app

words.js (full list, used to validate guesses)

common.js (short list, used to pick targets)

Regenerating the word files (after editing either .txt source):

php convert-words.php words.txt  words.js  WORD
php convert-words.php common.txt common.js COMMON

The third argument is what keeps the two files from colliding on global names — easy to forget.

The knobs worth remembering, all at the top of styles.css:

--app-width — overall page width (currently 30rem)

--cell, --cell-gap, --score-w — the tile grid

--board-min-rows — initial board height (currently 5)

--bg, --panel, --ink, --line, --good-*, --bad-* — the palette

In game.js: RECENT_LIMIT = 100 and RECENT_KEY = '5words.recentTargets' control the anti-repeat buffer.
